1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:06,817
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:10,195
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,322 --> 00:00:15,367
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:18,745
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,789 --> 00:00:23,709
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

6
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,627
But when the world needed him most,

7
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,004
he vanished.

8
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:31,216
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

9
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,884
an airbender named Aang.

10
00:00:32,969 --> 00:00:35,262
And although his
airbending skills are great,

11
00:00:35,346 --> 00:00:38,015
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

12
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:42,269
But I believe Aang can save the world.

13
00:01:08,129 --> 00:01:10,589
Great. You're back. What's for dinner?

14
00:01:10,673 --> 00:01:12,090
We've got a few options.

15
00:01:12,175 --> 00:01:16,178
First, round nuts and some kind of
oval-shaped nuts.

16
00:01:16,262 --> 00:01:19,556
And some rock-shaped nuts
that might just be rocks.

17
00:01:21,893 --> 00:01:23,393
Dig in.

18
00:01:23,603 --> 00:01:26,063
Seriously, what else you got?

19
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:35,989
What was that?

20
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,789
It's coming from over there.

21
00:01:43,873 --> 00:01:47,834
Shouldn't we run away from
huge booms, not toward them?

22
00:01:57,595 --> 00:01:58,595
Hyah.

23
00:01:58,679 --> 00:02:00,222
An earthbender.

24
00:02:00,306 --> 00:02:01,473
Let's go meet him.

25
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:04,017
He looks dangerous,
so we better approach cautiously.

26
00:02:04,227 --> 00:02:06,269
Hello there! I'm Katara.

27
00:02:06,479 --> 00:02:07,771
What's your name?

28
00:02:16,406 --> 00:02:17,989
Nice to meet you!

29
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,866
I just wanted to say hi.

30
00:02:20,076 --> 00:02:22,327
Hey, that guy's
got to be running somewhere.

31
00:02:22,537 --> 00:02:23,954
Maybe we're near a village.

32
00:02:24,038 --> 00:02:26,373
And I bet that village has a market.

33
00:02:26,457 --> 00:02:28,458
Which means no nuts for dinner.

34
00:02:28,543 --> 00:02:30,627
Hey! I worked hard to get those nuts.

35
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:33,505
Yeah, I hate them, too.

36
00:02:42,265 --> 00:02:43,473
Great hat.

37
00:02:43,558 --> 00:02:45,100
I'll trade you some nuts for it.

38
00:02:48,479 --> 00:02:49,855
Hey!

39
00:02:51,065 --> 00:02:52,190
Hi, Mom.

40
00:02:52,275 --> 00:02:53,483
Where have you been, Haru?

41
00:02:53,568 --> 00:02:54,568
You're late!

42
00:02:54,694 --> 00:02:56,403
Get started on your chores.

43
00:02:56,487 --> 00:02:58,280
Hey! You're that kid.

44
00:02:59,449 --> 00:03:00,490
Why did you run away before?

45
00:03:00,575 --> 00:03:03,368
You must have me confused
with some other kid.

46
00:03:03,786 --> 00:03:06,204
No, she doesn't.
We saw you earthbending.

47
00:03:08,416 --> 00:03:09,833
They saw you doing what?

48
00:03:10,042 --> 00:03:11,418
They're crazy, Mom.

49
00:03:11,502 --> 00:03:13,003
I mean, look at how they're dressed.

50
00:03:15,047 --> 00:03:17,340
You know how dangerous that is.

51
00:03:17,425 --> 00:03:20,635
You know what would happen
if they caught you earthbending.

52
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:22,053
Open up!

53
00:03:25,057 --> 00:03:26,683
Fire Nation. Act natural.

54
00:03:36,277 --> 00:03:37,694
Aah!

55
00:03:38,279 --> 00:03:41,198
What do you want?
I've already paid you this week.

56
00:03:41,282 --> 00:03:42,866
The tax just doubled.

57
00:03:43,075 --> 00:03:45,202
We wouldn't want an accident,
would we?

58
00:03:45,953 --> 00:03:49,539
Fire is sometimes so hard to control.

59
00:03:57,673 --> 00:03:59,633
You can keep the copper ones.

60
00:04:04,222 --> 00:04:05,430
Nice guy.

61
00:04:05,515 --> 00:04:07,307
How long has
the Fire Nation been here?

62
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:10,268
Five years. Fire Lord Ozai

63
00:04:10,353 --> 00:04:13,104
uses our town's coal mines
to fuel his ships.

64
00:04:13,314 --> 00:04:15,732
They're thugs. They steal from us.

65
00:04:15,816 --> 00:04:17,567
And everyone here
is too much of a coward

66
00:04:17,777 --> 00:04:18,902
to do anything about it.

67
00:04:18,986 --> 00:04:20,028
Quiet, Haru!

68
00:04:20,238 --> 00:04:21,571
Don't talk like that!

69
00:04:21,656 --> 00:04:23,031
But Haru's an earthbender.

70
00:04:23,115 --> 00:04:24,115
He can help.

71
00:04:24,325 --> 00:04:26,326
Earthbending is forbidden.

72
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:28,662
It's caused nothing
but misery for this village.

73
00:04:28,871 --> 00:04:31,122
He must never use his abilities.

74
00:04:31,541 --> 00:04:32,791
How can you say that?

75
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,584
Haru has a gift.

76
00:04:34,794 --> 00:04:36,211
Asking him not to earthbend

77
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,588
is like asking me not to waterbend.

78
00:04:38,673 --> 00:04:39,965
It's a part of who we are.

79
00:04:40,174 --> 00:04:41,758
You don't understand.

80
00:04:41,968 --> 00:04:44,928
I understand that Haru can help
you fight back.

81
00:04:45,012 --> 00:04:46,513
What can the Fire Nation do to you

82
00:04:46,597 --> 00:04:48,014
that they haven't done already?

83
00:04:48,099 --> 00:04:50,642
They could take Haru away,

84
00:04:50,851 --> 00:04:52,561
like they took his father.

85
00:05:00,736 --> 00:05:02,571
My mom said
you can sleep here tonight.

86
00:05:02,905 --> 00:05:04,656
But you should leave in the morning.

87
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:07,534
Thanks. I'll make sure
Appa doesn't eat all your hay.

88
00:05:13,457 --> 00:05:15,667
I'm sorry about
what I said earlier.

89
00:05:15,751 --> 00:05:17,210
I didn't know about your father.

90
00:05:17,295 --> 00:05:18,628
That's ok.

91
00:05:18,963 --> 00:05:22,257
It's funny. The way you were talking
back in the store,

92
00:05:22,341 --> 00:05:24,217
it reminded me of him.

93
00:05:24,302 --> 00:05:25,302
Thanks.

94
00:05:25,428 --> 00:05:27,012
My father was very courageous.

95
00:05:27,221 --> 00:05:28,972
When the Fire Nation invaded,

96
00:05:29,181 --> 00:05:31,600
he and the other earthbenders
were outnumbered ten to one.

97
00:05:31,809 --> 00:05:33,184
But they fought back anyway.

98
00:05:33,394 --> 00:05:35,186
He sounds like a great man.

99
00:05:36,105 --> 00:05:38,648
After the attack,
they rounded up my father

100
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:40,400
and every other earthbender

101
00:05:40,484 --> 00:05:43,486
and took them away.
We haven't seen them since.

102
00:05:43,738 --> 00:05:45,655
So that's why
you hide your earthbending.

103
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:46,740
Yeah.

104
00:05:47,742 --> 00:05:49,075
The problem is,

105
00:05:49,285 --> 00:05:52,662
the only way I can feel close
to my father now

106
00:05:52,747 --> 00:05:54,873
is when I practice my bending.

107
00:05:55,666 --> 00:05:57,917
He taught me everything I know.

108
00:05:59,837 --> 00:06:01,379
See this necklace?

109
00:06:01,589 --> 00:06:02,922
My mother gave it to me.

110
00:06:03,090 --> 00:06:04,299
It's beautiful.

111
00:06:04,383 --> 00:06:07,385
I lost my mother
in a Fire Nation raid.

112
00:06:07,470 --> 00:06:09,012
This necklace is all
I have left of her.

113
00:06:09,221 --> 00:06:11,222
It's not enough, is it?

114
00:06:11,307 --> 00:06:12,474
No.

115
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,230
Aah! Help!

116
00:06:19,315 --> 00:06:20,315
The mine!

117
00:06:20,399 --> 00:06:22,108
Aah...

118
00:06:23,402 --> 00:06:24,861
Help me!

119
00:06:31,202 --> 00:06:32,786
It's not working.

120
00:06:32,995 --> 00:06:34,162
We have to get help.

121
00:06:34,246 --> 00:06:36,790
There's no time. Pull harder!

122
00:06:36,874 --> 00:06:39,459
Haru, there's a way you can help him.

123
00:06:39,543 --> 00:06:40,794
I can't.

124
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,004
Please. There's no one around
to see you.

125
00:06:43,089 --> 00:06:44,464
It's the only way!

126
00:06:57,478 --> 00:06:58,728
Haru, you did it!

127
00:07:07,488 --> 00:07:09,864
It was so brave of Haru
to use his earthbending

128
00:07:09,949 --> 00:07:11,116
to help that old man.

129
00:07:11,659 --> 00:07:13,451
You must have really inspired him.

130
00:07:13,577 --> 00:07:14,577
I guess so.

131
00:07:14,787 --> 00:07:16,079
Everyone should get some sleep.

132
00:07:16,163 --> 00:07:17,247
We're leaving at dawn.

133
00:07:17,331 --> 00:07:19,290
Dawn? Can't we sleep in for once?

134
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:20,792
Absolutely not!

135
00:07:20,876 --> 00:07:22,919
This village is crawling
with Fire Nation troops.

136
00:07:23,129 --> 00:07:24,754
If they discover you're here, Aang,

137
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:26,339
we'll be eating fireballs
for breakfast.

138
00:07:26,549 --> 00:07:27,590
Good night.

139
00:07:28,008 --> 00:07:29,884
I'd rather eat fireballs than nuts.

140
00:07:29,969 --> 00:07:31,302
Good night.

141
00:07:55,119 --> 00:07:56,244
That's him!

142
00:07:56,328 --> 00:07:58,288
That's the earthbender!

143
00:07:58,372 --> 00:07:59,748
Aah!

144
00:08:28,152 --> 00:08:29,152
They took him!

145
00:08:29,361 --> 00:08:31,571
-They took Haru away!
-What?

146
00:08:31,655 --> 00:08:33,531
The old man turned him in
to the Fire Nation.

147
00:08:33,616 --> 00:08:35,909
It's all my fault.
I forced him into earthbending.

148
00:08:35,993 --> 00:08:38,578
Slow down, Katara.
When did this happen?

149
00:08:38,704 --> 00:08:41,456
Haru's mother said
they came for him at midnight.

150
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:43,208
Then it's too late to track him.
He's long gone.

151
00:08:43,292 --> 00:08:44,667
We don't need to track him.

152
00:08:44,752 --> 00:08:47,253
The Fire Nation is going to
take me right to Haru.

153
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,881
And why would they do that?

154
00:08:49,965 --> 00:08:53,176
Because they're going to arrest me
for earthbending.

155
00:08:56,263 --> 00:08:58,097
I thought you were
crazy at first, Katara,

156
00:08:58,182 --> 00:08:59,265
but this might work.

157
00:08:59,350 --> 00:09:01,476
There are ventilation shafts
throughout these mines.

158
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,228
All Aang has to do is
send an air current

159
00:09:03,312 --> 00:09:05,146
from that vent to this one right here.

160
00:09:05,231 --> 00:09:07,565
The boulder levitates and ta-da...

161
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:08,942
Fake earthbending.

162
00:09:09,026 --> 00:09:10,443
Aang, did you get all that?

163
00:09:10,528 --> 00:09:12,570
Sure, sure. I got it.

164
00:09:12,655 --> 00:09:14,155
Do you remember your cue?

165
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,241
Yeah, yeah. Just relax.

166
00:09:16,325 --> 00:09:18,159
You're taking all the fun out of this.

167
00:09:18,244 --> 00:09:20,829
By "this" do you mean
intentionally being captured

168
00:09:20,913 --> 00:09:22,747
by an army of ruthless firebenders?

169
00:09:22,832 --> 00:09:25,291
Exactly. That's fun stuff.

170
00:09:25,668 --> 00:09:27,919
Here they come.
Get in your places.

171
00:09:30,631 --> 00:09:32,924
Get out of my way, pipsqueak.

172
00:09:33,008 --> 00:09:37,512
How dare you call me pipsqueak,
you giant-eared cretin?

173
00:09:37,596 --> 00:09:39,138
What did you call me?

174
00:09:39,223 --> 00:09:41,266
A giant-eared cretin.

175
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:42,684
Look at those things.

176
00:09:42,768 --> 00:09:45,186
Do herds of animals
use them for shade?

177
00:09:45,271 --> 00:09:47,355
You better back off!

178
00:09:47,439 --> 00:09:48,606
Seriously, back off.

179
00:09:48,691 --> 00:09:50,483
I will not back off!

180
00:09:50,568 --> 00:09:52,068
I bet elephants get together

181
00:09:52,152 --> 00:09:55,029
and make fun of
how large your ears are.

182
00:09:55,114 --> 00:09:57,532
That's it! You're going down.

183
00:09:57,616 --> 00:09:59,868
I'll show you who's boss,

184
00:10:00,077 --> 00:10:02,453
earthbending style.

185
00:10:05,583 --> 00:10:09,168
I said, "earthbending style!"

186
00:10:13,007 --> 00:10:15,925
That lemur. He's earthbending.

187
00:10:17,845 --> 00:10:19,971
No, you idiot. It's the girl.

188
00:10:20,055 --> 00:10:22,432
Of course.

189
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:24,893
I'll hold her!

190
00:10:25,269 --> 00:10:27,228
You've got 12 hours
to find Haru.

191
00:10:27,313 --> 00:10:29,188
We'll be right behind you.

192
00:10:37,031 --> 00:10:39,532
Momo, you have some big ears.

193
00:11:18,113 --> 00:11:21,574
She'll be fine, Aang.
Katara knows what she's doing.

194
00:11:28,874 --> 00:11:32,710
Earthbenders,
it is my pleasure to welcome you

195
00:11:32,795 --> 00:11:35,046
aboard my modest shipyard.

196
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:37,548
I am your warden.

197
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:40,969
I prefer to think of you
not as prisoners,

198
00:11:41,053 --> 00:11:43,346
but as honored guests.

199
00:11:43,430 --> 00:11:45,640
And I hope you come to think of me

200
00:11:45,724 --> 00:11:49,394
as your humble and caring host.

201
00:11:49,478 --> 00:11:52,605
You will succeed here
if you simply abide...

202
00:11:55,693 --> 00:11:56,859
Hyah!

203
00:11:58,570 --> 00:12:02,490
What kind of guest dishonors his host
by interrupting him?

204
00:12:02,574 --> 00:12:03,992
Take him below.

205
00:12:04,201 --> 00:12:08,037
One week in solitary
will improve his manners.

206
00:12:08,122 --> 00:12:11,666
Simply treat me with the courtesy
I give you

207
00:12:11,750 --> 00:12:15,336
and we'll get along famously.

208
00:12:15,504 --> 00:12:17,755
You will notice, earthbenders,

209
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:21,259
that this rig is made
entirely of metal.

210
00:12:21,385 --> 00:12:25,304
You are miles away
from any rock or earth.

211
00:12:25,389 --> 00:12:28,474
So, if you have any illusions
about employing

212
00:12:28,559 --> 00:12:31,728
that brutish savagery
that passes for bending

213
00:12:31,812 --> 00:12:34,731
among you people, forget them.

214
00:12:35,482 --> 00:12:38,026
It is impossible.

215
00:12:39,069 --> 00:12:40,445
Good day.

216
00:13:05,846 --> 00:13:07,138
Katara?

217
00:13:07,222 --> 00:13:08,347
Haru!

218
00:13:08,432 --> 00:13:09,515
What are you doing here?

219
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,976
It's my fault you were captured.

220
00:13:12,186 --> 00:13:13,644
I came to rescue you.

221
00:13:13,854 --> 00:13:15,646
So you got yourself arrested?

222
00:13:15,814 --> 00:13:17,690
It was the only way to find you.

223
00:13:17,775 --> 00:13:20,234
You've got guts, Katara.
I'll give you that.

224
00:13:20,444 --> 00:13:23,321
Come on. There's someone
I want you to meet.

225
00:13:24,782 --> 00:13:27,450
Katara, this is my father, Tyro.

226
00:13:28,285 --> 00:13:30,703
Dad, this is Katara.

227
00:13:30,788 --> 00:13:32,080
It's an honor to meet you.

228
00:13:33,957 --> 00:13:35,541
Have some dinner, Katara.

229
00:13:36,877 --> 00:13:37,877
Ew.

230
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,046
It's not as bad as it looks.

231
00:13:42,508 --> 00:13:43,633
Eew!

232
00:13:43,717 --> 00:13:45,635
It's still pretty bad, though.

233
00:13:45,719 --> 00:13:47,345
Tyro, the prisoners are complaining

234
00:13:47,429 --> 00:13:49,263
there aren't enough blankets
to go around.

235
00:13:49,348 --> 00:13:50,932
I'll talk to the guards.

236
00:13:51,016 --> 00:13:53,976
In the meantime, make sure
the elderly are taken care of.

237
00:13:54,061 --> 00:13:56,729
The rest of us will simply have to
hope for warmer weather.

238
00:13:56,814 --> 00:13:58,231
If you don't mind me asking,

239
00:13:58,315 --> 00:13:59,524
what's your escape plan?

240
00:13:59,608 --> 00:14:00,608
Excuse me?

241
00:14:00,859 --> 00:14:03,319
You know, the plan
to get everyone off the rig?

242
00:14:03,403 --> 00:14:05,113
What is it? Mutiny, sabotage?

243
00:14:05,197 --> 00:14:08,324
The plan? The plan is to survive,

244
00:14:08,408 --> 00:14:10,952
wait out this war, hope that one day

245
00:14:11,036 --> 00:14:13,871
some of us can get back home
and forget this ever happened.

246
00:14:13,956 --> 00:14:15,832
How can you say that?

247
00:14:15,916 --> 00:14:17,416
You sound like
you've already given up.

248
00:14:17,626 --> 00:14:20,419
Katara, I admire your courage.

249
00:14:20,504 --> 00:14:22,588
And I envy your youth.

250
00:14:22,798 --> 00:14:25,216
But people's lives are at stake here.

251
00:14:25,425 --> 00:14:27,552
The warden is a ruthless man,

252
00:14:27,636 --> 00:14:29,971
and he won't stand for any rebellion.

253
00:14:30,222 --> 00:14:33,099
I'm sorry, but we're powerless.

254
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,684
We'll see about that.

255
00:14:38,814 --> 00:14:40,523
Earthbenders!

256
00:14:40,607 --> 00:14:43,317
You don't know me, but I know of you.

257
00:14:43,402 --> 00:14:46,654
Every child in my water tribe village
was rocked to sleep

258
00:14:46,738 --> 00:14:49,073
with stories of the brave
Earth Kingdom

259
00:14:49,283 --> 00:14:52,201
and the courageous earthbenders
who guard its borders.

260
00:14:52,744 --> 00:14:54,787
Some of you may think
that the Fire Nation

261
00:14:54,872 --> 00:14:56,330
has made you powerless.

262
00:14:56,707 --> 00:14:59,584
Yes. They have taken away
your ability to bend.

263
00:14:59,668 --> 00:15:02,086
But they can't take away your courage.

264
00:15:02,171 --> 00:15:04,589
And it is your courage
they should truly fear,

265
00:15:04,673 --> 00:15:07,008
because it runs deeper than any mine

266
00:15:07,092 --> 00:15:08,551
you've been forced to dig,

267
00:15:08,635 --> 00:15:11,220
any ocean that keeps you
far from home.

268
00:15:11,305 --> 00:15:13,139
It is the strength of your hearts

269
00:15:13,223 --> 00:15:14,724
that make you who you are,

270
00:15:14,808 --> 00:15:18,186
hearts that will remain unbroken
when all rock and stone

271
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:19,478
has eroded away.

272
00:15:19,688 --> 00:15:22,190
The time to fight back is now!

273
00:15:22,399 --> 00:15:25,484
I can tell you
the Avatar has returned!

274
00:15:25,569 --> 00:15:27,737
So remember your courage,
earthbenders!

275
00:15:27,821 --> 00:15:30,239
Let us fight for our freedom!

276
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,400
Shh.

277
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:11,822
Your 12 hours are up. Where is Haru?

278
00:16:11,907 --> 00:16:13,115
We've got to get out of here.

279
00:16:13,575 --> 00:16:15,034
I can't.

280
00:16:15,118 --> 00:16:17,536
We don't have much time.
There are guards everywhere.

281
00:16:17,621 --> 00:16:18,913
Get on!

282
00:16:19,122 --> 00:16:20,706
Katara, what's wrong?

283
00:16:20,958 --> 00:16:22,416
I'm not leaving.

284
00:16:23,752 --> 00:16:26,003
I'm not giving up on these people.

285
00:16:31,718 --> 00:16:33,344
What do you mean,
you're not leaving?

286
00:16:33,428 --> 00:16:35,513
We can't abandon these people.

287
00:16:35,597 --> 00:16:37,223
There has to be a way to help them.

288
00:16:37,307 --> 00:16:40,226
Maybe she's right.
What do you say, Sokka?

289
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:41,894
I say you're both crazy.

290
00:16:43,814 --> 00:16:46,190
Last chance. We need to leave now.

291
00:16:46,525 --> 00:16:47,525
No.

292
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:50,278
I hate when you get like this.

293
00:16:50,362 --> 00:16:51,737
Come on, we better hide.

294
00:16:53,782 --> 00:16:54,782
Go.

295
00:16:59,162 --> 00:17:00,413
Look!

296
00:17:01,164 --> 00:17:03,916
Tell me exactly what you saw.

297
00:17:04,001 --> 00:17:05,918
Well, sir, it looked like
a flying bison.

298
00:17:06,003 --> 00:17:07,003
What?

299
00:17:07,212 --> 00:17:09,005
It was a giant, flying buffalo, sir,

300
00:17:09,089 --> 00:17:10,131
with an empty saddle.

301
00:17:10,215 --> 00:17:13,175
Which was it, a buffalo or a bison?

302
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:16,053
I'm not sure what the difference is,

303
00:17:16,138 --> 00:17:18,097
but that's not really the point,
is it, sir?

304
00:17:18,181 --> 00:17:21,225
I'll decide what the point is, fool!

305
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:23,477
Aah!

306
00:17:24,938 --> 00:17:28,858
You! Wake up the captain!
Search the entire rig!

307
00:17:28,942 --> 00:17:30,234
-Sir.
-What?

308
00:17:30,319 --> 00:17:33,779
That was the captain
you just threw overboard, so...

309
00:17:33,864 --> 00:17:36,198
Then wake up someone
I haven't thrown overboard

310
00:17:36,283 --> 00:17:37,616
and search the rig.

311
00:17:37,701 --> 00:17:40,786
There's something going on here,
and I don't like it.

312
00:17:48,337 --> 00:17:51,255
We don't have much time.
What are we gonna do?

313
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,174
I wish I knew how to make a hurricane.

314
00:17:54,676 --> 00:17:57,261
The warden would run away,
and we would steal his keys.

315
00:17:57,429 --> 00:17:59,680
Wouldn't he just
take his keys with him?

316
00:17:59,765 --> 00:18:01,849
I'm just tossing ideas around.

317
00:18:01,933 --> 00:18:03,100
I tried talking the earthbenders

318
00:18:03,185 --> 00:18:05,644
into fighting back,
but it didn't work.

319
00:18:05,729 --> 00:18:08,731
If there was just a way
to help them help themselves.

320
00:18:08,815 --> 00:18:12,318
For that they need some kind of
earth or some rock,

321
00:18:12,861 --> 00:18:14,320
something they can bend.

322
00:18:14,404 --> 00:18:16,113
But this entire place
is made of metal.

323
00:18:19,242 --> 00:18:21,118
No, it's not. Look at the smoke.

324
00:18:21,995 --> 00:18:24,038
I bet they're burning coal.

325
00:18:24,122 --> 00:18:25,498
In other words...

326
00:18:25,749 --> 00:18:27,041
Earth.

327
00:18:30,712 --> 00:18:33,381
It's almost dawn.
We're running out of time.

328
00:18:33,465 --> 00:18:34,965
You sure this is gonna work?

329
00:18:35,092 --> 00:18:36,175
It should.

330
00:18:36,259 --> 00:18:37,843
These vents reminded me
of our little trick

331
00:18:37,928 --> 00:18:39,095
back at the village.

332
00:18:39,179 --> 00:18:42,223
We're gonna do the same thing,
but on a much bigger scale.

333
00:18:42,307 --> 00:18:45,017
There's a huge deposit of coal
at the base of this island.

334
00:18:45,102 --> 00:18:46,811
And the whole system is ventilated.

335
00:18:46,895 --> 00:18:49,105
Aang closed off
all the vents except one.

336
00:18:49,189 --> 00:18:50,398
When he does his airbending,

337
00:18:50,482 --> 00:18:52,191
the coal only has one place to go...

338
00:18:52,275 --> 00:18:53,442
Right back here.

339
00:18:53,652 --> 00:18:55,277
There's the intruder!

340
00:18:55,487 --> 00:18:57,446
Stay back! I'm warning you!

341
00:18:57,656 --> 00:19:00,616
Katara, stop.
You can't win this fight.

342
00:19:03,286 --> 00:19:05,621
Listen to him well, child.

343
00:19:05,831 --> 00:19:07,706
You're one mistake away

344
00:19:07,791 --> 00:19:10,084
from dying where you stand.

345
00:19:30,689 --> 00:19:32,815
Here's your chance, earthbenders!

346
00:19:33,024 --> 00:19:35,484
Take it!
Your fate is in your own hands!

347
00:19:44,411 --> 00:19:45,828
Foolish girl.

348
00:19:46,037 --> 00:19:48,622
You thought a few inspirational words

349
00:19:48,832 --> 00:19:52,293
and some coal
would change these people?

350
00:19:52,377 --> 00:19:56,422
Look at these blank hopeless faces.

351
00:19:56,506 --> 00:19:59,508
Their spirits were broken
a long time ago.

352
00:19:59,718 --> 00:20:03,179
But you still believed in them.

353
00:20:03,263 --> 00:20:05,431
How sweet.

354
00:20:05,515 --> 00:20:09,101
They're a waste of your energy,
little girl.

355
00:20:09,186 --> 00:20:11,645
You failed.

356
00:20:15,609 --> 00:20:16,650
Grr.

357
00:20:18,695 --> 00:20:19,695
Hyah!

358
00:20:25,702 --> 00:20:27,244
Show no mercy!

359
00:20:30,165 --> 00:20:31,832
Aah!

360
00:20:31,917 --> 00:20:32,958
For the Earth Kingdom,

361
00:20:33,043 --> 00:20:34,418
attack!

362
00:21:10,038 --> 00:21:12,289
Get to the ship! We'll hold them off!

363
00:21:12,374 --> 00:21:14,166
Do not let them escape!

364
00:21:17,546 --> 00:21:19,296
Guys, throw me some coal!

365
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:36,605
No, please. I can't swim.

366
00:21:36,690 --> 00:21:39,316
Don't worry. I hear cowards float.

367
00:21:49,953 --> 00:21:52,246
I want to thank you for saving me,

368
00:21:52,330 --> 00:21:53,622
for saving us.

369
00:21:53,832 --> 00:21:55,666
All it took was a little coal.

370
00:21:55,875 --> 00:21:58,168
It wasn't the coal, Katara.

371
00:21:58,253 --> 00:21:59,712
It was you.

372
00:21:59,921 --> 00:22:02,423
Thank you for helping me
find my courage,

373
00:22:02,507 --> 00:22:04,174
Katara of the water tribe.

374
00:22:04,384 --> 00:22:06,927
My family and everyone here

375
00:22:07,137 --> 00:22:08,887
owes you much.

376
00:22:09,097 --> 00:22:11,432
So, I guess you're going home now.

377
00:22:11,516 --> 00:22:14,059
Yes, to take back my village.

378
00:22:14,269 --> 00:22:16,478
To take back all of our villages!

379
00:22:16,688 --> 00:22:18,731
The Fire Nation will regret the day

380
00:22:18,815 --> 00:22:20,691
they set foot on our land!

381
00:22:21,985 --> 00:22:23,152
Come with us.

382
00:22:23,236 --> 00:22:24,361
I can't.

383
00:22:24,571 --> 00:22:26,322
Your mission
is to take back your home.

384
00:22:26,531 --> 00:22:30,075
Ours is to get Aang to the North Pole.

385
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:32,202
That's him, isn't it? The Avatar.

386
00:22:34,998 --> 00:22:38,042
Katara, thank you for bringing
my father back to me.

387
00:22:38,126 --> 00:22:40,294
I never thought I'd see him again.

388
00:22:40,378 --> 00:22:42,046
I only wish there was some way...

389
00:22:42,255 --> 00:22:43,881
I know.

390
00:22:43,965 --> 00:22:46,467
My mother's necklace! It's gone!
